      "writtenOn": "2026-04-03T01:49:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, I see your point.\n\nI\u0027d be fine with either squashing it or reordering it, my intention here is just to help us _remember_ to reorder it specifically before or after \"pKVM: VMX: Implement TLB flush for guest EPT\" (or squash into it) during a future rebase.\n\nSo we might just add mentioning that specific commit here, either in the form of a Fixes: tag or just as a note?\n\n(BTW my understanding is that a Fixes: tag means simply: we\u0027ve had a bug because of the given patch, and now we are fixing this bug; it doesn\u0027t necessarily mean we should squash the fix into that exact patch.)",
